<!--
  IL2CPP managed code stripping at Medium or High removes types and fields that are only ever
  reached by reflection. Every model the SDK sends to JsonUtility is exactly that: the fields
  are populated by name, never referenced in code. Stripped, the dialog silently falls back to
  bundled English copy - on the customer's device build only, never in the editor, which is the
  worst possible place for it to first appear.

  The models also carry [Preserve]. This file is the belt to that pair of braces: it keeps the
  whole assembly, which is under a thousand lines and costs nothing worth measuring.

  Unity collects link.xml from packages as well as from Assets, so this needs no registration.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="PromptSurge.Runtime" preserve="all" />
</linker>
